        "original_id": "1a592256-304a-504d-b0e3-5c1d228d60bf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Gangkhar Puensum, Jongsong Peak, Bhutan\n- Concepts: mountain height rankings, unclimbed mountains, elevation, prominence\n\nFacts:\n- Gangkhar Puensum is the highest mountain in Bhutan.\n- Gangkhar Puensum has an elevation of 7,570 meters and a prominence of 2,995 meters.\n- Gangkhar Puensum is a strong candidate for the highest unclimbed mountain in the world.\n- Jongsong Peak has an elevation of 7,462 meters.\n- Jongsong Peak is the 57th highest peak in the world.\n- Kangchenjunga is the 3rd highest mountain in the world and lies 20 kilometers south of Jongsong Peak.\n- Kangchenjunga dominates Jongsong Peak.",
